2026-09-04T00:00:00Z (RFD66606-2200) 'ReBAC agent roles as tuples, not per-agent policy sprawl
 # uuid: 8fe9ea6c-8d54-54b7-9124-175373b9b2b6
 # tags: rfd:title
 RFD:Discussion  1 RFD
 Serials:VSekaiFabric

2026-09-04T00:00:01Z (RFD66606-2200) 'relationship tuples in Bao KV under `relationships/` define agent roles and what they can and cannot do
 # tags: rfd:feature, rfd:no-final-newline
 Text:RFD2200  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-04T00:00:02Z (RFD66606-2200) 'Bao coordination store, all live agents, future onboarding flow
 # tags: rfd:scope, rfd:no-final-newline
 Text:RFD2200  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-04T00:00:03Z (RFD66606-2200) 'Agent roles are relationship tuples in Bao KV, not per-agent policies.
 # tags: rfd:hook
 Text:RFD2200  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-04T00:00:04Z (RFD66606-2200) 'The current `agents-rw` policy is one shared grant across every peer. Adding a fourth agent that shouldn't touch GPU code, or a Hailo-specific agent that must not touch the 3090, means either a new per-agent policy (RBAC sprawl) or ad-hoc restrictions in prose.
 # tags: rfd:intrigue
 Text:RFD2200  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-04T00:00:05Z (RFD66606-2200) 'Run `mix rfd.rebac` to hold every rebac block in the corpus against the verb vocabulary.
 # tags: rfd:exit
 Text:RFD2200  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-04T00:00:06Z (RFD66606-2200) 'ReBAC agent roles as tuples, not per-agent policy sprawl
 # tags: rfd:details-title, rfd:no-final-newline
 Text:RFD2200  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-04T00:00:07Z (RFD66606-2200) 'Model agent roles as **ReBAC relationship tuples** in a Bao KV mount at `relationships/`, one tuple per row, key shape `<subject>--<verb>--<object>`. This RFD owns the verb vocabulary and declares it in a `rebac` block (RFD66606-2291, ReBAC as a DSL feature), so the verbs are data rather than a table a gate parses. Three named roles fall out: coordinator (MPS), gpu-experimenter (CUDA), edge-qat-specialist (HAILO). `DETAILS.md` carries verbs, rows, scopes.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2200  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-04T00:00:08Z (RFD66606-2200) 'RFD66606-2195 (Bao PKI + agent-provisioning discipline), agent-sync skill in dot-claude.
 # tags: rfd:related
 Text:RFD2200  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-04T00:00:09Z (RFD66606-2200) 'Non-goals
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2200  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-04T00:00:10Z (RFD66606-2200) 'Not enforced today. The tuples are data; nothing gates a KV write against them yet. When enforcement lands it goes in a separate RFD. Also not covered: an external ReBAC engine (OpenFGA, SpiceDB). The tuples-in-KV shim is the minimum that answers the question we have. A production ReBAC engine is a future call.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2200  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-04T00:00:11Z (RFD66606-2200) 'The tuple shape
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2200  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-04T00:00:12Z (RFD66606-2200) 'Each tuple is one KV row under `relationships/`. Key format is `<subject>--<verb>--<object>` (double-hyphen separator, all segments lowercase-kebab). Data is the parsed fields plus a timestamp:
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2200  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-04T00:00:13Z (RFD66606-2200) '    subject: mps-45994b
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2200  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-04T00:00:14Z (RFD66606-2200) '    verb: authors
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2200  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-04T00:00:15Z (RFD66606-2200) '    object: weftspun-agreements
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2200  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-04T00:00:16Z (RFD66606-2200) '    created_at: <unix>
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2200  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-04T00:00:17Z (RFD66606-2200) 'The verb vocabulary is below, one `verb` declaration per row. It is small on purpose. A new verb is a `verb` line in this RFD before it is a row anywhere; overloading an existing verb is fine when the mapping is obvious.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2200  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-04T00:00:18Z (RFD66606-2200) 'A row whose verb carries a `!` is a denial: `<subject>--!<verb>--<object>` says the subject does not hold the relation, and it carries its reason after `#`. Default deny already covers what no row names; a denial row answers a question an agent would otherwise have to ask.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2200  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-04T00:00:19Z (RFD66606-2200) 'Tuples in a document
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2200  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-04T00:00:20Z (RFD66606-2200) '`AGENTS.md` carries the desk agent's tuples in a fenced `rebac` block, one row per line, with a note or a reason after `#`. The block is rendered from the `renders_into "AGENTS.md"` rows declared here, so the document holds no second copy to drift from.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2200  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-04T00:00:21Z (RFD66606-2200) '`mix rfd.rebac` holds every block in the corpus against the vocabulary, and `scripts/check_rebac.exs` holds `CLAUDE.md` against it on its own. Both read `RFD.ReBAC`, so a verb no RFD declares fails, and so does a denial without its reason, a repeated row, or a relation both granted and denied.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2200  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-04T00:00:22Z (RFD66606-2200) 'The three roles
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2200  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-04T00:00:23Z (RFD66606-2200) '**Coordinator**, MPS. Bao admin (`mps-admin` policy). Authors `weftspun-agreements` (CLAUDE.md, RFDs, doctrine, retraction pointers). Provisions agent identities on operator instruction. Drafts logbook entries **only** when relaying a peer's measurement, with the peer credited as the measuring session. Does not own ML hypotheses; does not run GPU experiments; does not touch peer hardware.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2200  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-04T00:00:24Z (RFD66606-2200) '**GPU-experimenter**, CUDA. Owns 3090 + 4090. Authors `gpu-experiments`, Lumina2 distillation, LLaDA-o step sweeps, OmniGen2 comparisons, EditScore ladder runs. Publishes measurements as logbook PRs on its own branches; drafts + files its own retractions when a result doesn't survive scale-up. `agents-rw` policy; no admin ops (no mint, no revoke, no policy edit).
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2200  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-04T00:00:25Z (RFD66606-2200) '**Edge-QAT-specialist**, HAILO. Owns USB-Hailo NPU. Authors `edge-qat-experiments`, RFD66606-2199 direction, HailoRT + DFC compiler work, HEF deployment. Same PR-driven measurement discipline as gpu-experimenter. `agents-rw` policy; does not touch CUDA's cards, and CUDA does not touch the Hailo NPU, even though both agents `runs-on` the same `windows-desktop`.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2200  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-04T00:00:26Z (RFD66606-2200) 'What the tuples buy that RBAC doesn't
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2200  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-04T00:00:27Z (RFD66606-2200) '**Composability.** "CUDA touches the 3090" is not a permission written into a policy; it is `cuda-a63415 owns desktop-3090` and a general rule "an agent's `owns` relations bound the hardware it can drive." Adding a fourth agent that inherits GPU access means adding `<new>--owns-- <card>`, not editing a policy.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2200  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-04T00:00:28Z (RFD66606-2200) '**Cross-cutting constraints from graph traversal.** The shared-$HOME risk that killed CUDA's key earlier today is graph-reachable:
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2200  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-04T00:00:29Z (RFD66606-2200) '    ?x runs-on ?h  AND  ?y runs-on ?h  AND  ?x != ?y
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2200  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-04T00:00:30Z (RFD66606-2200) 'resolves to `(cuda-a63415, hailo-552dfa, windows-desktop)`. A future onboarding flow can check "does this new agent share a host with an existing agent?" mechanically from the tuples, and if so require the per-agent-suffixed cred dir before enrolment. RBAC has no way to express that.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2200  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-04T00:00:31Z (RFD66606-2200) '**Retraction responsibility.** When an RFD is retracted, the doctrine in CLAUDE.md says the pointer names the logbook entry that carries the measurement. `authored-by` tuples on the RFD and the logbook entry resolve to the same agent, so the pointer's target is not a lookup; it is the second tuple that shares a subject with the first.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2200  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-04T00:00:32Z (RFD66606-2200) 'What the tuples do not do today
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2200  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-04T00:00:33Z (RFD66606-2200) 'No policy consults them. `agents-rw` still writes based on identity templating, not tuple membership. This RFD lands the **schema and the tuples**, not enforcement.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2200  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-04T00:00:34Z (RFD66606-2200) 'Enforcement would need one of:
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2200  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-04T00:00:35Z (RFD66606-2200) '1. **Client-side check in the agent-sync skill.** Read `relationships/*` on startup, memoise, refuse local operations that would violate a tuple relation. Cheap; only as strong as agent cooperation.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2200  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-04T00:00:36Z (RFD66606-2200) '2. **Bao Sentinel or a custom auth method** that consults `relationships/` before granting a write. Requires either Bao Enterprise or a shim.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2200  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-04T00:00:37Z (RFD66606-2200) '3. **A separate ReBAC engine** (OpenFGA, SpiceDB, Zanzibar-alike) as the source of truth; Bao KV becomes cache. Correct long-term shape at the cost of a second service.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2200  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-04T00:00:38Z (RFD66606-2200) 'None of the three ships in this RFD. The tuples come first because storing the relationships is the small commitment that any of the three build on. Enforcement is a separate call and a separate RFD.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2200  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-04T00:00:39Z (RFD66606-2200) 'The extend flow
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2200  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-04T00:00:40Z (RFD66606-2200) 'Adding a new agent:
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2200  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-04T00:00:41Z (RFD66606-2200) '1. Operator authorises identity (per RFD66606-2195 rule zero).
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2200  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-04T00:00:42Z (RFD66606-2200) '2. Admin (MPS) mints cert, publishes bundle to `certs/<cn>`.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2200  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-04T00:00:43Z (RFD66606-2200) '3. **Admin writes the new agent's tuples to `relationships/`** in the same session, at minimum a `runs-on` tuple, plus the `owns` and `authors` tuples that scope the new agent's role.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2200  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-04T00:00:44Z (RFD66606-2200) '4. If a `runs-on` shares a host with an existing agent, admin confirms the new agent will use a per-agent-suffixed cred dir before completing onboarding.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2200  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-04T00:00:45Z (RFD66606-2200) '5. Agent writes its first KV row to `agents/<cn>.agents.weftspun`.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2200  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-04T00:00:46Z (RFD66606-2200) 'Removing an agent (revocation):
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2200  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-04T00:00:47Z (RFD66606-2200) '1. Admin revokes cert per RFD66606-2195's Revocation section.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2200  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-04T00:00:48Z (RFD66606-2200) '2. Admin deletes tuples where the revoked agent is `subject` (its claims stop being active) but preserves tuples where the revoked agent is `object` (so `windows-desktop hosts cuda-a63415` survives if we're just revoking CUDA, and the tuple gets deleted on the same step as CUDA's other row cleanups).
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2200  1 LINE
 Text:Written

